From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Broyojo <dha@xoba.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:49:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] hw/net/mlx5: striding RQ, multi-packet send, memory keys,
 inventory registers

Bring the data path and the port's self-description in line with what a
ConnectX-5 offers by default:

 - Memory keys with MTT, KSM and KLM translation tables, created with
   CREATE_MKEY and updated by UMR work queue entries.  Every address in a
   work queue entry is now resolved through its key.
 - Striding (multi-packet) receive queues, which the driver prefers over
   the scatter-list ones, including filler completions.
 - Enhanced multi-packet send WQEs.
 - CQE compression may be enabled; the device never chooses to compress.
 - Long transmit bursts are continued from a bottom half so that one busy
   queue does not hold up the rest of the machine.
 - Port registers: the full set of ConnectX-5 link modes with speed
   selection and autonegotiation state, FEC (PPLM), the cable's module
   EEPROM (MCIA, a QSFP28 passive copper cable), and the PCAM/MCAM
   capability masks.  Management registers: firmware component version
   (MCQS/MCQI) and a temperature sensor (MTCAP/MTMP).

